# fmt — real-world examples

## Split long lines only, leave short lines alone

```sh
fmt -s services
```

## Wrap a text file to 72 columns

```sh
fmt -w 72 notes.txt
```

## Reflow a README to 80 columns and save the result

```sh
fmt -w 80 README > README.new && mv README.new README
```

## Reflow pasted text from stdin

```sh
cat brain-dump.txt | fmt -w 66
```

## Uniform spacing — one space between words, two after sentences

```sh
fmt -u draft.txt
```

| Flag | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| -w N | wrap at N columns (default 75) |
| -s | split long lines, don't join short ones |
| -u | uniform spacing |
| -p PREFIX | only reflow lines starting with PREFIX (e.g. `#` comments) |
